From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: convert theme nonclient font points to logical pixels

The INI font parser returns point sizes. Applying that positive LOGFONT
height leaves live system font caches using the cell height in pixels,
while a registry reload converts it to a negative point-derived height.
Use the same conversion as theme property fonts before setting unaware
nonclient metrics. Caption, menu, dialog and icon fonts keep their sizes
across live theme changes and relaunch. The appearance probe checks both
architecture variants at the console target of 96 logical DPI.

--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -796,6 +796,11 @@
     if (SUCCEEDED (MSSTYLES_GetFont (lpValue, lpValue + dwValueLen, &lpValue,
         &font)))
     {
+        /* Theme INI sizes are points, while LOGFONT passed to SPI is in
+         * logical pixels. Positive cached heights otherwise draw tiny fonts
+         * until registry reload converts them, changing appearance on restart.
+         * parse_apply_nonclient uses the 96-DPI unaware coordinate space. */
+        font.lfHeight = -MulDiv( font.lfHeight, USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI, 72 );
         switch (iPropertyId)
         {
 	  case TMT_CAPTIONFONT:
